\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{The energy at the edge of a square}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{In the [finite spatial chain](fdip-00GV), each bond penalizes a
difference of field values. A bond from a retained site to a fixed zero
value penalizes that site's value itself. At a corner of a square, two
such penalties remain even though only two neighbors are retained.
How should the [Gaussian precision](fdip-0005) express this boundary
energy together with a fixed physical square and its changing mesh?}
